of Katrina evacuee students received by school j in grade g and year t,
and some controls. This regression is a three-way fixed effects version
of Regression 1. The stable groups assumption is satisfied: there are
schools that did not receive any Katrina evacuee. This a fuzzy design:
the treatment of interest is the proportion of evacuees in
\end{quote}

20

\begin{quote}
one's class, which varies within (school,grade,year) cells.
